# libbwt89

A strict-ISO-C89, green-compliant, dependency-free library of Burrows-Wheeler
transform (BWT) variants over arbitrary bytes.

## Variants

| Variant | Forward | Inverse | Notes |
|---------|---------|---------|-------|
| Regular | `bwt89_bwt` | `bwt89_ibwt` | Classic transform + LF inverse. Reports a 0-based row `index`; no sentinel byte is emitted, so output length equals input. |
| Bijective | `bwt89_bbwt` | `bwt89_ibbwt` | The transform is a permutation of the input (same multiset, no index). Byte-for-byte validated against the OpenBWT `BWTS` / `UnBWTS` oracle. |
| Dynamic | *(planned)* | *(planned)* | Incremental insert/delete/substitute edits of a maintained transform without full recompute. |

## API

`include/bwt89.h` declares the public surface in the `bwt89_` namespace.

```c
enum bwt89_status
{
    BWT89_OK = 0,
    BWT89_NULL_ARG,   /* a required pointer is NULL */
    BWT89_NOMEM,      /* internal allocation failed */
    BWT89_BAD_INDEX,  /* regular-ibwt index out of range */
    BWT89_BAD_EDIT    /* reserved for the future dynamic module */
};

enum bwt89_status bwt89_bwt (const unsigned char *s, size_t n,
                             size_t *index, unsigned char *out);
enum bwt89_status bwt89_ibwt(const unsigned char *b, size_t n,
                             size_t index, unsigned char *out);
enum bwt89_status bwt89_bbwt(const unsigned char *s, size_t n,
                             unsigned char *out);
enum bwt89_status bwt89_ibbwt(const unsigned char *b, size_t n,
                              unsigned char *out);
```

- Inputs/outputs are **caller-owned, length-prefixed byte buffers**
  (`const unsigned char *` + `size_t`). Binary data and embedded NUL bytes are
  valid input.
- Every transform writes exactly `n` bytes (a permutation of the input).
  `bwt89_bbwt` needs no index; `bwt89_ibbwt` inverts it. `bwt89_bwt` stores the
  0-based row of the original text in `*index` (range `0..n`); `bwt89_ibwt`
  takes that `index` back.
- The library may allocate O(n) internal scratch and report `BWT89_NOMEM`; it
  never requires the caller to allocate workspace.
- Errors: a `NULL` required pointer -> `BWT89_NULL_ARG`; an `index` outside
  `[0, n]` -> `BWT89_BAD_INDEX`; allocation failure -> `BWT89_NOMEM`. Caller
  buffers are not left partially overwritten on these paths.

## Example

```c
#include <bwt89.h>

unsigned char in[]  = "the quick brown fox";
unsigned char b[18];
unsigned char out[18];
size_t index;

bwt89_bwt(in, 18, &index, b);     /* forward  */
bwt89_ibwt(b, 18, index, out);    /* inverse  */
/* out now equals in */
```

## Building, testing, and the green gate

The repository uses [`just`](https://github.com/casey/just). Run recipes from
the project root:

- `just build` — compile every `src/*.c` under strict flags and archive
  `build/libbwt89.a`.
- `just smoke` — build and run the end-to-end smoke test.
- `just unit` — build and run each unit test in `test/unit/`.
- `just test` — `smoke` first, then `unit`.
- `just green` (alias `just check`) — generate GCC/Clang compilation databases
  and run the sibling `green` driver's seven-cell matrix (strict C89/C23 for
  GCC and Clang, clang-tidy semantic checks, canonical Allman format).
- `just lint` — `shellcheck` on scripts and `clang-format --dry-run` on C.
- `just format` — rewrite sources to canonical formatting.
- `just doctor` — verify all required external tools are present.
- `just clean` — remove `build/`.

Strict compile flags: `-std=c89 -pedantic-errors -Wall -Wextra -Werror
-Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wstrict-prototypes -Wmissing-prototypes
-Wold-style-definition -Wundef -Wshadow -Wformat=2`.

The `green` driver defaults to `../../green/.agent/tmp/build/green`; override with
`GREEN=...`. See `green.yaml` for the pure-function and toolchain profile.

## Source layout

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `include/bwt89.h` | Public API and status codes. |
| `src/bwt89_sa.c` | Linear-time SA-IS suffix array over an integer alphabet. |
| `src/bwt89_bwt.c` | Regular `bwt` / `ibwt`. |
| `src/bwt89_bwts.c` | Bijective `bbwt` / `ibbwt` (Duval Lyndon factorization + conjugate sort). |
| `src/bwt89_internal.h` | Shared internal prototypes. |
| `test/` | Smoke test plus unit suite per concern. |
| `.agent/` | Concept, stories, design, BDD testing scenarios, and acceptance documents. |

## Conventions

- Strict ISO C89, four-space indent, Allman braces, 80-column limit
  (`.clang-format`).
- Same source is warning-clean as strict C89 and C23 under both GCC and Clang,
  plus the green semantic checks (the "green source profile").
- Functional style, most functions short (2-7 lines); no function-like macros;
  no owned type names ending in `_t`.
- No dependency beyond the C89 standard library.

## Verified against an independent oracle

The bijective transform is byte-for-byte equal to Yuta Mori's canonical
OpenBWT `BWTS`, and its inverse to `UnBWTS`, over thousands of randomized and
structured inputs. The reference vector `bwt89_bbwt("banana")` is
`"annbaa"`. Sanity vectors `abc -> cab`, `aab -> baa`, `aaab -> baaa`, and
`^BANANA$ -> $ANNBAA^`.

